title: "earthchange: Multipurpose satellite environmental monitoring and change detection"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21370696"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21370696"
    description: "Concept DOI (all versions)"
abstract: >-
  Pure-Python toolkit for satellite environmental monitoring and change
  detection, spanning 24 scenarios from free public archives. Hazard: fire
  danger from the Canadian Fire Weather Index on Indonesian (BMKG/ASEAN)
  thresholds, and drought. Impact: burned area, floods, deforestation, mining,
  urbanisation, surface-water and coastal change (erosion/accretion with
  cross-shore rates in m/yr), multi-epoch urban and population growth,
  land-surface heat. Exposure and accountability: smoke exposure in person-days
  by air-quality class with age structure, air-parcel trajectories (kinematic or
  NOAA ARL HYSPLIT, forward and backward), and reproducible per-zone fire-season
  records. Runs on Google Earth Engine or Microsoft Planetary Computer (no
  account needed). Produces georeferenced GeoTIFFs, quick-look PNGs, statistics,
  print-ready maps, citable Markdown records, and an assembled brief. Each
  output carries its own stated limits. Formerly published as "satchange".
